Projects/UOContent/Mobiles/Guards/BaseGuard.cs

Adds the static event BaseGuard.Killing, raised by the guard's attack timer just before it kills its focus outright,
while the target is still whole: who it was fighting and who struck it can still be read. Also names the guard as
LastKiller before Kill(). Without this patch BotAIv2 does not compile (BotHaven subscribes to the event).

WHY. Build 429, 07-08.10.2026: the guards killed none of 78 creatures that chased a bot into town, and the bots
could not tell a guard's kill from any other. Damage names the killer only when the blow goes below zero, and
HitsMax on a creature at full health leaves it at exactly zero, so the Kill() that follows killed it with no killer
named. BotHaven counts a guard's kill as a rescue of the bot the creature was fighting, which needs both.

diff --git a/Projects/UOContent/Mobiles/Guards/BaseGuard.cs b/Projects/UOContent/Mobiles/Guards/BaseGuard.cs
index 1fe8c89ac..86ffaf651 100644
